nodecode-vaultknox is a rewrite of Ufonik88's Ufonik88/Hermes-VaultKnox:

https://github.com/Ufonik88/Hermes-VaultKnox
commit 8aea272fd9b071615fcd0c93a38b760485673316
Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Ufonik (LICENSE)

The plugin is Python: a registry of 28 secret detectors, three Hermes hooks
that redact a message on its way in, inject secret-handling rules, and rewrite a
reply that asks the user for a key, and a tool that reads an encrypted vault
when the vaultknox package is installed. This rewrite keeps the registry and
the policy and drops the Python. The detectors are the plugin's own cl-ppcre
patterns, one to one, matched over every message of a request at the point the
event log is folded into provider-shaped messages -- a copy is rewritten, the
log keeps the original -- and an assistant turn is passed through the same
secret-asking rewrite, now advice to keep the value out of chat rather than a
command line for the vault. Left out: the encrypted vault itself and its tool
actions (masked references, one-time tokens, write gates, token revocation),
which a local sealed store already covers in Nodecode, so this cell only scans
and redacts; the per-conversation injection of secret-handling rules, which is
a system-prompt habit here rather than a rewritten turn; the unsalted SHA-256
fingerprint the plugin logged beside each finding; and the placeholder's
rotation notice, which stays in the tool's answer and this folder's README.
